# =============================================================================
# @alkemio/test-suite-server-api — environment template. Copy to `.env`.
# Uncomment ONE environment block; secrets are placeholders — fill them in.
# =============================================================================

# --- LOCAL (default) ---------------------------------------------------------
AUTH_TEST_HARNESS_PASSWORD=change_me
KRATOS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:3000/ory/kratos/public
ALKEMIO_SERVER=http://localhost:3000/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
ALKEMIO_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
ALKEMIO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
MAIL_SLURPER_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4437/mail
ALKEMIO_SERVER_WS=ws://localhost:3000/graphql
ALKEMIO_SERVER_REST=http://localhost:3000/api/private/rest
SKIP_USER_REGISTRATION=false
TRAVIS=false
# RabbitMQ management HTTP API (compose publishes 15672) — emit-level assertions
# for internal queues (e.g. alkemio-push-notifications) that have no GraphQL
# surface. Endpoint/user match server/quickstart-services.yml's rabbitmq
# service; take the password from there (or from the k8s secret
# alkemio-rabbitmq-cluster-default-user against a cluster) — never commit it.
RABBITMQ_MANAGEMENT_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:15672
RABBITMQ_MANAGEMENT_USER=alkemio-admin
RABBITMQ_MANAGEMENT_PASSWORD=change_me
# Messaging digest windows (034-messaging-notifications / Operator Ruling R4).
# Messaging notifications are debounced per (recipient, channel, kind) track and
# then digested, so every messaging wait in the suites is derived from these —
# see lib/src/utils/messaging-digest-windows.ts (`digestWindow`). Required by
# src/functional-api/notifications/messaging/*.it-spec.ts.
# These MUST match what the SERVER under test is configured with: the same nine
# variables are read by the server (data-model.md §6). The production in-code
# defaults are minutes-scale (60/300/300/1800 s ...); the seconds-scale values
# below are what a local/CI verification stack should run so the suites finish
# in minutes rather than hours. If a variable is unset the harness falls back to
# the PRODUCTION default, never to the short value — a negative assertion must
# never pass just because the dispatch has not happened *yet*.
MESSAGING_DIGEST_PUSH_DIRECT_QUIET_SECONDS=2
MESSAGING_DIGEST_PUSH_DIRECT_MAX_DELAY_SECONDS=10
MESSAGING_DIGEST_PUSH_GROUP_QUIET_SECONDS=3
MESSAGING_DIGEST_PUSH_GROUP_MAX_DELAY_SECONDS=12
MESSAGING_DIGEST_EMAIL_DIRECT_QUIET_SECONDS=4
MESSAGING_DIGEST_EMAIL_DIRECT_MAX_DELAY_SECONDS=15
MESSAGING_DIGEST_EMAIL_GROUP_QUIET_SECONDS=6
MESSAGING_DIGEST_EMAIL_GROUP_MAX_DELAY_SECONDS=20
MESSAGING_DIGEST_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1

# --- TEST (test-alkem.io) ----------------------------------------------------
# AUTH_TEST_HARNESS_PASSWORD=change_me
# KRATOS_ENDPOINT=https://identity.test-alkem.io/ory/kratos/public
# ALKEMIO_SERVER=https://test-alkem.io/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_URL=https://test-alkem.io/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
# ALKEMIO_BASE_URL=https://test-alkem.io
# MAIL_SLURPER_ENDPOINT=https://test-alkem.io/mailslurper-api/mail
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_WS=wss://test-alkem.io/graphql
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_REST=https://test-alkem.io/api/private/rest
# SKIP_USER_REGISTRATION=true

# --- DEV (dev-alkem.io) ------------------------------------------------------
# AUTH_TEST_HARNESS_PASSWORD=change_me
# KRATOS_ENDPOINT=https://identity.dev-alkem.io/ory/kratos/public
# ALKEMIO_SERVER=https://dev-alkem.io/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_URL=https://dev-alkem.io/api/private/non-interactive/graphql
# ALKEMIO_BASE_URL=https://dev-alkem.io
# MAIL_SLURPER_ENDPOINT=https://dev-alkem.io/mailslurper-api/mail
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_WS=wss://dev-alkem.io/api/private/ws
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_REST=https://dev-alkem.io/api/private/rest
# SKIP_USER_REGISTRATION=true

# --- Messaging digest windows: which values belong where ---------------------
# The nine MESSAGING_DIGEST_* above are read by BOTH the harness and the server,
# and they must carry the SAME values on both sides. Set them here but not on
# the server, and every wait is measured against a window the server is not
# using — which is worse than not setting them at all.
#
#   Track           Production (quiet / cap)   Local + CI (quiet / cap)
#   push  direct       60s /  300s                 2s /  10s
#   push  group       300s /  900s                 3s /  12s
#   email direct      300s / 1800s                 4s /  15s
#   email group      1200s / 3600s                 6s /  20s
#   sweep interval     10s                         1s
#
# Production is what real users experience; the seconds-scale column is what a
# local or ephemeral CI stack should run so the suites finish in minutes.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS ON A HOSTED ENV (test-alkem.io, dev-alkem.io): as of this
# writing these variables are NOT declared on any deployment (Operator Ruling
# R3), so those servers run the PRODUCTION windows above. Do NOT copy the
# seconds-scale values into a hosted block — the harness would then wait 6s,
# see nothing, and pass a negative assertion whose dispatch is still ~59
# minutes away. Leaving them unset is correct: the harness falls back to the
# production defaults and waits accordingly. It is also slow — a single
# `email:group` negative assertion costs maxDelay + sweep + settle ~= 61 min,
# which is why only the cheapest specs are nightly-eligible against a hosted
# env today. See https://github.com/alkem-io/test-suites/issues/605.
#
# RabbitMQ management is ClusterIP-only on a cluster (no public ingress, by
# design): reach it with `kubectl port-forward svc/alkemio-rabbitmq-cluster
# 15672:15672` and point RABBITMQ_MANAGEMENT_ENDPOINT at localhost.
# --- Server prerequisite: non-interactive-login (post-OIDC auth) -------------
# The harness authenticates by POSTing credentials to
#   {ALKEMIO_BASE_URL}/api/auth/non-interactive-login
# which the SERVER must have enabled, or token acquisition fails with HTTP 404.
#   • Local server: set these in the SERVER's own env (NOT here):
#       ENABLE_NON_INTERACTIVE_LOGIN=true
#       NON_INTERACTIVE_LOGIN_SIGNING_KEY=<32+ random bytes, hex or base64>
#     (requires a non-production NODE_ENV; the server refuses to start in prod)
#   • test-alkem.io / dev-alkem.io: the platform team enables it server-side.
# The harness reads no new variable for this — it reuses ALKEMIO_BASE_URL and
# AUTH_TEST_HARNESS_PASSWORD from the active block above.

# --- Environment guard (identity-provisioning safety) ------------------------
# Before provisioning/registering/minting any test identity, globalTestsSetup
# checks every configured endpoint above (ALKEMIO_SERVER, ALKEMIO_BASE_URL,
# ALKEMIO_SERVER_WS, ALKEMIO_SERVER_REST, MAIL_SLURPER_ENDPOINT,
# KRATOS_ENDPOINT, KRATOS_PRIVATE_API_URL, and KRATOS_ADMIN_URL when set)
# against an allowlist of approved throwaway hosts — see
# lib/src/config/environment-guard.ts. localhost/127.0.0.1 and the
# test-alkem.io / dev-alkem.io families are approved; anything else (including
# acceptance/production hosts) aborts the run before any identity is touched.
#
# If you are deliberately standing up a genuinely new test/dev environment not
# yet covered by that allowlist, opt out explicitly — never as a default, never
# committed to a real .env file:
# ALLOW_UNAPPROVED_TEST_TARGET=yes-i-understand
